From b8e65c4bdb17d085daeb55c1368389bc35239386 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): skip empty moe_swiglu_cast slabs and restore
 post-gate shared_experts hook

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
1. In vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/moe.py, moe_swiglu_cast launched rows_per_cta = 4 if warps >= 4 else 2 (only 2 rows/CTA on TP3 where intermediate = 768 and warps = 3, doubling active-tile slabs from 4 to 8), unconditionally preloaded all rows_per_cta Order and Weights entries before pdl.chain(), and after pdl.chain() stepped through every row r in 0..rows_per_cta-1 inside an unrolled loop even when orders[0] < 0 (an empty slab, which represents 75% of active-tile CTAs in decode since active experts average 1.0-2.1 rows out of 16) or orders[1] < 0 (a 1-row tile, which represents 68%-100% of slab == 0 CTAs in decode).
   Use rows_per_cta = 2 if intermediate > 1152 else 4 so TP3 (intermediate = 768) also processes 4 rows/CTA; cascade Order and Weights preloads before pdl.chain() so empty slabs only read orders[0] and 1-row tiles only read orders[0..1] and weights[0]; exit empty slabs immediately after pdl.chain() via if expert >= 0 and orders[0] >= 0:; and guard rows 1..rows_per_cta-1 behind if rows_per_cta > 1 and orders[1] >= 0:.
2. In vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/runner/moe_runner.py, _forward_impl checked workspace_size == 0 and launched shared_experts.maybe_forward_async before _apply_quant_method even when fold_shared == True (where workspace_size == 0 is always true because shared experts accumulate directly into the routed combine buffer). That bypassed the decode router._post_gate_hook in _apply_quant_method and launched shared_experts on the side stream before router gate GEMM, causing SM contention with the router gate GEMM and cold-L2 FFN prefetch. Furthermore, when _post_gate_hook fired after partials_kernel, maybe_forward_async recorded _input_ready_event on current_stream() after partials_kernel, forcing the side stream to wait for partials_kernel before starting shared_experts.
   Skip the pre-_apply_quant_method shared_experts launch when fold_shared is True, pre-record _input_ready_event before router.select_experts when deferring shared_experts to _post_gate_hook, and add input_ready_recorded=True to SharedExpertsRunner.maybe_forward_async so the side stream only waits on hidden_states readiness while still launching after router gate GEMM.

Quality:
Bit-identical (torch.equal, 0 uint16 diffs, max_abs_diff == 0.0) across all TP4 and TP3 shapes (M = 1..48), both standalone and end-to-end inside captured decode CUDA graphs.

Tests:
- pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_l2_schedule.py tests/kernels/moe/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_moe.py tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_pdl.py (160 passed across 2 boots).

Upstream status: local DeepSeek V4.1 TileLang MoE and dual-stream runner optimization for GB10.
